1) What is Pagination
      Pagination is a technique used to retieve data page by page instead of loading all records at once from the database.
                                    or
      Pagination is a feature in Spring Boot used to fetch large amounts of data in smaller chunks called oages. It improbes performance 
      and reduce memory usage. Spring Data JPA provides pagination using pageable, PageRequest, and Page interfaces.

2) DTO  ( Data Transfer Object )
      DTO is an object used to transfer data betwee client and server without exposing the actual entity class.

      Why DTO
      ------
            We use DTO to transfer only the required data between client and server. It improves security by hiding sensitive fields, reduces
            data transfer and decouples the API layer from the database entity layer.

3) DTO pattern
      DTO is a design pattern used to transfer data between layers of an application, especially between the Client <-> Controller <-> Service <-> Database.
      Why do we use DTO?
      -----------------
           - Hide sensitive data (like password).
           - Send only required fields to the client.
           - Reduce data transfer size.
           - Separate API response structure from database entities.



















